@page "/products/leasing"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Serga Leasing"; ViewData["Description"] = "Connect leased operational assets with suppliers, locations, agreements, costs and end dates."; }
<section class="hero container detail-hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Serga Leasing</p><h1>Every leased asset.<br /><em>Always under control.</em></h1><p class="hero-description">Know what you lease, where it is, what it costs and when the agreement ends. Keep the asset and its commercial context together.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/platform">Explore the platform <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><partial name="_LeasingMockup" /></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The equipment behind the operation</p><h2>Basic questions.<br /><em>Connected answers.</em></h2><p>Across locations and teams, spreadsheets make it difficult to understand which equipment is leased, who supplies it and when a decision is due.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>Asset & location</h3><p>Connect vehicles, machinery, printers, production equipment and technical equipment to the place they are used.</p></article><article><h3>Supplier & agreement</h3><p>Keep the supplier and covering agreement with the asset, including the commercial terms and supporting documents.</p></article><article><h3>Cost & next decision</h3><p>Track the cost context, end dates and renewal decisions across the leased estate.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The lease lifecycle</p><h2>From arrival<br /><em>to the next decision.</em></h2><p>Follow a leased delivery vehicle from its first assignment to the commercial decision at the end of its term.</p></div><ol class="workflow"><li><span class="eyebrow">01</span><strong>Lease begins</strong><p>Capture the supplier and agreed commercial terms.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">02</span><strong>Asset registered</strong><p>Identify the equipment and the agreement covering it.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">03</span><strong>Location assigned</strong><p>Connect the asset to the responsible organization and location.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">04</span><strong>Costs tracked</strong><p>Keep cost commitments with the leased equipment.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">05</span><strong>End date approaches</strong><p>Review renewal or termination options in time.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">06</span><strong>Decision required</strong><p>Record whether to renew, return or replace the asset.</p></li></ol></section>

<section class="context-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Independently useful. Better together.</p><h2>Operational clarity.<br /><em>Commercial context.</em></h2><p>Leasing works on its own, with the asset, supplier, location and agreement context needed to understand each lease.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>No Contracts dependency</h3><p>An asset can carry its agreement context within Leasing. A separate Contracts product is not required.</p></article><article><h3>Coexist with operations</h3><p>Keep maintenance and specialist technical work in the appropriate operational systems; connect relevant business context where possible.</p></article><article><h3>Optional wider relationships</h3><p>Contracts adds a broader agreement view. Services can connect the customer-facing service context around the equipment.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Make the connection</p><h2>Know the assets<br /><em>you depend on.</em></h2><a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span class="cta-tagline">Your gateway to services</span></div></section>
